Chromium [caches http credentials](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:net/http/http_auth_cache.h;l=26-33;drc=cc67230216085a28c28177f5601fb3079198f774) per `origin + realm + scheme`, where:
- `origin` is scheme+host+port of the request;
- `realm` is the auth realm;
- `scheme` is the auth scheme.

See [WWW-Authenticate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/WWW-Authenticate#directives) for realm/scheme descriptions.

We should do the same with our API - specify `origin` instead of `hostname`. If it is easy to add optional `realm`/`scheme` fields for all browsers, we can also do that.
